# Security & Configuration

## Environment Variables
- `.env*` files are gitignored; Turbo `build` task declares `.env*` as inputs
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` — required by `OpenAIEmbedder` in `packages/memory/src/openai-embedder.ts`; read from `process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY` or passed via constructor options
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` — web dashboard API base; defaults to `http://localhost:4000`; used in `apps/web/app/lib/api.ts`

## Secrets Handling
- No secrets in source — `.env*`, `*.pem` are gitignored
- `OpenAIEmbedder` constructor: `new OpenAIEmbedder({ apiKey?: string })` — falls back to `process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY`
- Never log or persist API keys in event payloads or `EventLog` rows (they are broadcast via WebSocket)

## Data Storage (gitignored)
- SQLite database: `apps/backend/data/farm.db` (Prisma datasource: `file:../data/farm.db`; `apps/backend/data/` gitignored)
- Runtime memory: `.bot-ville/` at repo root (JSON files for knowledge base, agent state, task tracking, history)
- JSON fields in SQLite stored as strings — `WorkOrder.context`, `Task.deps`, `EventLog.payload` are `String` columns; `PrismaAdapter` helper methods handle `JSON.parse()`/`JSON.stringify()`

## API Route Security

### Mutating routes (`/api/*`) — desktop app only
Defined in `apps/backend/src/routes/api.ts` via `registerApiRoutes()`:
- `POST /api/work-orders` — create work order
- `POST /api/work-orders/:id/tasks` — create task
- `POST /api/work-orders/:id/tick` — run engine tick
- `POST /api/work-orders/:id/merge` — request merge
- `POST /api/work-orders/:id/decisions` — record decision
- `POST /api/tasks/:id/assign` — assign task to role
- `POST /api/tasks/:id/status` — update task status
- `POST /api/tasks/:id/artifact` — submit artifact

### Read-only routes (`/public/*`) — web dashboard only
Defined in `apps/backend/src/routes/public.ts` via `registerPublicRoutes()`:
- `GET /public/work-orders` — list work orders
- `GET /public/work-orders/:id` — get snapshot (work order + tasks + artifacts + decisions + events)
- `GET /public/work-orders/:id/tasks` — list tasks
- `GET /public/work-orders/:id/artifacts` — list artifacts
- `GET /public/events` — query events (supports `workOrderId`, `role`, `action`, `since`, `limit`, `offset` params)
- `GET /public/health` — health check
- `GET /public/agents` — list agent sessions (optional `?status=` filter)
- `GET /public/project` — project context
- **Guard**: `onRequest` hook rejects non-GET/HEAD/OPTIONS with 405: `"The /public/* endpoints are read-only. Only GET requests are permitted."`

### Agent routes
Defined in `apps/backend/src/routes/agents.ts` via `registerAgentRoutes()`:
- `POST /api/agents/spawn` — spawn agent session
- `POST /api/agents/:id/heartbeat` — agent heartbeat
- `POST /api/agents/:id/done` — mark agent completed
- `POST /api/agents/:id/kill` — kill agent
- `GET /api/agents` — list sessions
- `POST /api/agents/:id/mail` — send mail

### WebSocket endpoint
Defined in `apps/backend/src/routes/ws.ts` via `registerWsRoute()`:
- `ws://localhost:4000/ws` — streams all `EventBus` events
- Client sends `{ type: "subscribe", filters: { workOrderId?, role?, action? } }` to filter
- Desktop hook (`apps/desktop/src/renderer/src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts`) buffers up to 500 events client-side and auto-reconnects every 2 seconds on disconnect

### General
- No authentication layer currently — security boundary is route prefix separation (`/api/*` vs `/public/*`)
- CORS enabled via `@fastify/cors` with `{ origin: true }`

## Electron Security
- Context isolation enabled — renderer cannot access Node.js APIs directly
- `contextBridge` preload exposes a limited `electronAPI` surface:
  - `openDirectoryDialog()` — opens native directory picker via `dialog.showOpenDialog`
  - `getWebDashboardInfo()` — returns web dashboard URL and port
  - `ipc.send(channel, ...args)` — one-way IPC to main process
  - `ipc.on(channel, callback)` — listen for IPC from main process
  - `ipc.invoke(channel, ...args)` — request/response IPC
- Main process IPC handlers: `dialog:open-directory`, `web:get-info`

## Agent Isolation
- Each spawned agent runs in its own git worktree managed by `WorktreeManager` (`packages/core/src/agents/worktree.ts`)
- Worktree created via `WorktreeManager.create({ repoRoot, roleId, taskId?, sessionId, baseBranch? })`
- Agent sessions track `pid`, `workingDirectory`, `status`, and `lastHeartbeat`
- `AgentSpawner.kill(sessionId)` terminates process and updates status
- `AgentSpawner.prune()` cleans up stale sessions (no heartbeat, process exited)
- `WorktreeManager.remove()` / `removeWithBranch()` cleans up worktree directory and branch
